NV_PK(1,{"milkfish is tainan's everyday fish a famous folk legend explains its name in 1661 when koxinga's army landed in tainan fishermen offered him a shiny silver fish in his accent he asked what fish is this and locals heard sat ba hi the fish's taiwanese name today that is why it is also called koxinga's fish":"","tainan's coastal fish farms have raised milkfish for more than three hundred years the fish eats algae and has soft delicate meat but it also has over two hundred tiny bones tainan cooks became masters at removing them even from the bony belly":"","tainan people eat every part milkfish belly congee with a fried dough stick for breakfast fish skin soup for lunch and pan fried fish intestine head or braised skin later in the day":"","milkfish":"","milkfish cannot stand the cold cold snaps can kill whole ponds so they are farmed mainly in warm southern taiwan":"","in tainan people eat milkfish congee for breakfast":"","could you remove the bones for me":"","the belly is the softest part of the fish":"","a silver fish with many small bones farmed in ponds in southern taiwan":"","tainan people eat milkfish for breakfast":"","legend":"","an old story that many people tell but nobody can prove":"","legend says koxinga named this fish":"","bone":""});